2714 \nQ 2189 2714 2253 2829 \nL 2342 2829 \nz\n\" transform=\"scale(0.015625)\"></path></defs><use xlink:href=\"#STIXGeneral-Italic-73\" transform=\"translate(0 0.796875)\"></use></g></g><g id=\"text_8\"><!-- $\\mathit{k}$ --><g transform=\"translate(7.2 23.34995) scale(0.13 -0.13)\"><defs><path id=\"STIXGeneral-Italic-6b\" d=\"M 2950 2739 \nL 2950 2637 \nQ 2720 2624 2464 2448 \nQ 2208 2272 1510 1651 \nL 1747 1088 \nQ 2099 262 2266 262 \nQ 2400 262 2554 531 \nQ 2586 582 2650 698 \nL 2746 627 \nQ 2522 224 2374 77 \nQ 2227 -70 2035 -70 \nQ 1894 -70 1782 42 \nQ 1670 154 1517 454 \nQ 1325 826 1133 1357 \nL 877 1152 \nL 570 0 \nL 90 0 \nL 992 3379 \nQ 1082 3699 1107 3942 \nQ 1088 4096 781 4096 \nL 666 4096 \nL 666 4198 \nQ 1146 4256 1670 4371 \nL 1709 4333 \nL 941 1414 \nL 1216 1626 \nQ 2131 2330 2131 2522 \nQ 2131 2637 1894 2637 \nL 1805 2637 \nL 1805 2739 \nL 2950 2739 \nz\n\" transform=\"scale(0.015625)\"></path></defs><use xlink:href=\"#STIXGeneral-Italic-6b\" transform=\"translate(0 0.703125)\"></use></g></g></g></g><defs><clipPath id=\"pe4939fe293\"><rect x=\"16.711364\" y=\"20.772678\" width=\"209.25\" height=\"207.9\"></rect></clipPath></defs></svg>\n<div role=\"region\" aria-label=\"Long description for diagram of 3 lines\" class=\"sr-only\"><ul>\n<li>Clockwise from top left, the 3 lines are labeled k, r, and s.</li>\n<li>Line k intersects both line r and line s.</li>\n<li>At the intersection of line k and line r, 2 angles are labeled clockwise from top left as follows:<br>\n<ul>\n<li>Top right: w°</li>\n<li>Bottom right: x°</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>At the intersection of line k and line s, 2 angles are labeled clockwise from top left as follows:<br>\n<ul>\n<li>Top right: y°</li>\n<li>Bottom right: z°</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>A note indicates the figure is not drawn to scale.</li>\n</ul></div></figure></p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">In the figure shown, line <math alttext=\"k\"><mi>k</mi>\n</math> intersects lines <math alttext=\"r\"><mi>r</mi>\n</math> and <math alttext=\"s\"><mi>s</mi>\n</math>. If <math alttext=\"w equals 147\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>w</mi>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mn>147</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math>, which additional piece of information is sufficient to prove that lines <math alttext=\"r\"><mi>r</mi>\n</math> and <math alttext=\"s\"><mi>s</mi>\n</math> are parallel?</p>", "keys": ["bd5ea3aa-77dd-4eb6-aacd-ba7589e62dc9"], "answerOptions": [{"id": "d4b0e6d1-3a88-49bf-bd75-0377d113a957", "content": "<p style=\"text-align: left;\"><math alttext=\"x equals 33\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mn>33</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math></p>"}, {"id": "bd5ea3aa-77dd-4eb6-aacd-ba7589e62dc9", "content": "<p style=\"text-align: left;\"><math alttext=\"y equals 147\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>y</mi>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mn>147</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math></p>"}, {"id": "1098e46f-d8e2-47ca-a265-9bdf5c6db781", "content": "<p style=\"text-align: left;\"><math alttext=\"w plus y equals 180\"><mrow>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mi>w</mi>\n\t\t<mo>+</mo>\n\t\t<mi>y</mi>\n\t</mrow>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mn>180</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math></p>"}, {"id": "313aa54a-cccc-4bac-a2e2-01b25c10a76e", "content": "<p style=\"text-align: left;\"><math alttext=\"y plus z equals 180\"><mrow>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mi>y</mi>\n\t\t<mo>+</mo>\n\t\t<mi>z</mi>\n\t</mrow>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mn>180</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math></p>"}], "rationale": "<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice B is correct. The figure shows transversal <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"k\"><mi>k</mi></math> intersecting lines <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"r\"><mi>r</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"s\"><mi>s</mi></math>, where the angles labeled <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"w degree\"><mi>w</mi><mo>&#176;</mo></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"y degree\"><mi>y</mi><mo>&#176;</mo></math> are two corresponding angles and the angles labeled <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"x degree\"><mi>x</mi><mo>&#176;</mo></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"z degree\"><mi>z</mi><mo>&#176;</mo></math> are two corresponding angles. When a transversal intersects two lines, the lines are parallel if and only if two corresponding angles are congruent. It&rsquo;s given that <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"w equals 147\"><mi>w</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>147</mn></math>. If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"y equals 147\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>147</mn></math>, then the two corresponding angles labeled <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"w degree\"><mi>w</mi><mo>&#176;</mo></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"y degree\"><mi>y</mi><mo>&#176;</mo></math> are congruent, which is sufficient to prove that lines <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"r\"><mi>r</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"s\"><mi>s</mi></math> are parallel.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice A is incorrect. The angle labeled <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"x degree\"><mi>x</mi><mo>&#176;</mo></math> forms a linear pair with the angle labeled <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"w degree\"><mi>w</mi><mo>&#176;</mo></math>, so <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"x equals 180 minus 147\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>180</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>147</mn></math>, or <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"x equals 33\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>33</mn></math>, regardless of whether lines <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"r\"><mi>r</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"s\"><mi>s</mi></math> are parallel.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice C is incorrect. Substituting <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"147\"><mn>147</mn></math> for <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"w\"><mi>w</mi></math> in this equation yields <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"147 plus y equals 180\"><mn>147</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>180</mn></math>, or <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"y equals 33\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>33</mn></math>. Since the angle labeled <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"w degree\"><mi>w</mi><mo>&#176;</mo></math> and the angle labeled <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"y degree\"><mi>y</mi><mo>&#176;</mo></math> are corresponding angles, if <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"w\"><mi>w</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"y\"><mi>y</mi></math> aren&rsquo;t equal, then lines <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"r\"><mi>r</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"s\"><mi>s</mi></math> can&rsquo;t be parallel.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice D is incorrect. The relationship <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"y plus z equals 180\"><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>180</mn></math> describes a linear pair at line <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"s\"><mi>s</mi></math>, which is true regardless of whether lines <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"r\"><mi>r</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"s\"><mi>s</mi></math> are parallel.</p>", "externalid": "86d8b279-9fd7-4afb-97df-f463761e3ebe", "correct_answer": ["B"]}